PROJECT_DIR=$(dirname "$0")
BLOG_TITLE="welcome back"
BG="../assets/bg.jpg"
BLOG_DATE="2026-11-20"

init

source $PROJECT_DIR/src/extensions/blogpost.ibke

ptop
paragraph "hello! it's me, kevadesu."
paragraph "this is a new edition of my blog :p"
paragraph "i acknowledge that i'm ass at blogging, so expect some low quality posts on this blog."
paragraph "as to why i decided to name the blog...\"segmentation success\"? i..honestly don't know :sob: i tried to pick a name that sounds cool, but in the end i feel like it might sound corny/edgy to some :/ but that's besides the point!"
paragraph "i'm more excited about telling you with what i'm writing this blog!!"
paragraph "i'm using an SSG which literally no one other than me has heard of: <a href=\"https://github.com/ibikei\">ibikei!</a>"
paragraph "it's an SSG i made myself, with a sort of...markup/programming language i made for it too? (IBK-Lang)"
paragraph "the fun part is, any bash code is valid IBK-Lang. this gives me like, endless possibilities!"
paragraph "look, you can even see what system i last built the blog from (updated every time the blog is recompiled btw:)"
uname -a >> $IBK_OUT
t "<br>"
paragraph "or you can even see on which date and time i last updated the blog as a whole :P"
date >> $IBK_OUT
t "<br>"
paragraph "if you're curious on how this works, you can take a look into my blog's repository <a href=\"https://github.com/kevadesu/myblog\">right here</a>, where you can see the source .ibkx files and stuff"
paragraph "anyways, i don't really have much more in mind that i can write in this blog post, but i welcome you to a new beginning!"
paragraph "i also hope you, the reader, will enjoy reading the blog posts as much as i enjoy writing them!!!"
pbottom